Z||000000||RossT||02-16-2001||03:09 AM||||My t-top car did not come with the t-top straps installed in the trunk. I was able to find a NOS strap kit (thanks fieroparts.com).<P>But I am going to need some help from someone that has the straps. I have the only t-top car in the state, so I just can't go look at another car.<P>1. My strap kit does not have the bolts, so I first need to know what size bolts to use.<BR>length and head size (is it metric?) Do they also use a washer?<P>2. Next I need to know where to drill the holes in the trunk. Looks like there are three spots. How far from the sides and/or bottom/top of the trunk?<P>Posting several pics of your trunk straps would be greatly apprecitated.<P>Thanks for you help!<P>strapless!!!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||02-16-2001||04:21 AM||||Ross,<P>I will look at my T-Top GT later today and will try to take some pictures.  All I have is an el cheapo digital camera, so I'm not sure if I will be able to take very detailed shots.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||02-16-2001||04:27 AM||||Thanks Mrfiero!! <P>One last question, When drilling thru the trunk wall, do I have to worry about any wires?  I know that there is a small false space or gap.  Thats where the dome light wires pass.<P><BR>Ross<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||02-16-2001||04:56 AM||||I don't think you'll have any worries about wires, but I'll have to wait until I see my GT before I can be certain.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||02-16-2001||10:17 PM||||Why bother?  I've never used my straps.  The Glass fits behind the seats nicely.  Easy and quick storage and access.  And you don't have to worry about theft either.  How many other t-top fieros owners are you ever going to cross paths with and would they really ever steal your tops?||||reg||5
Z||000005||mrfiero||02-16-2001||10:39 PM||||Ross,<P>The straps on the GT I have aren't bolted down.  The hole for the top part is right below the trunk light......there are no wires there, so don't worry.  The other two holes are in the corners of the trunk floor (upper part closest to the front of the car).  I forgot to  bring the camera, so I have no pics.<P>Tom,<P>Ross' GT has less than 1000 miles on it (at least last time I heard) and I'm guessing that he wants it to be as it "should" be.....that is with the straps installed.<P><p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 02-16-2001).]||||reg||1
